it's the most populous country in the  world with over 1.4 billion people  living here but believe it or not china  has a population problem  here's why  with a population bigger than north  america and europe combined  you wouldn't necessarily think china's  leaders would be worried about how many  people live there  a recent census revealed it has a  population of 1.41 billion people  but the rate of growth is slowing and  more worryingly  the number of babies being born is going  down  in 2020 12 million babies were born over  2 million fewer than the 14.66 million  in 2019.  the population decline hasn't always  been a concern of the chinese government  in fact  previously they welcomed it  [Music]  china has controlled how many children  people can have for decades  the infamous one child policy was first  introduced in 1979  as a way of stopping rapid population  growth outpacing economic development  this was policed with huge fines and  even forced abortions  it led to a huge gender imbalance in  china with many parents choosing to have  an abortion  or even abandon their child if it wasn't  a boy as of 2020  they're around 35 million more males  than females in china  the one child policy was relaxed in 2015  and the government began to allow  families to have two children  but this policy isn't the only reason  the birth rate is so low  [Music]  um  many experts have actually blamed just  how expensive it is to raise a child in  china  housing education and food can cost a  lot in the country  especially in the big cities  so now the government has relaxed the  rules even further and introduced a  three-child policy on its own  probably not the two-child policy did  lead to a short-term increase in the  birth rate  that didn't last very long and reaction  online to the three-child policy  announcement was chilly at best  a poll on sinha's weibo account asked  their followers if they were ready for  the three child policy  and 29 000 people out of the 31 000 who  replied  clicked the never even think of it  option the poll was quickly taken  offline  it is shocking that in 2021 china has  still so much control over women's  bodies  but you could argue that those controls  have been too successful  generations are now used to having small  families in china and as shown in 2015  changing the rules won't necessarily  work  on  the government is trying other things to  stop the aging population  they have promised to increase the  retirement age which will be unpopular  and to expand the pension system which  will be expensive  it isn't the first country to face this  population problem the current fertility  rate is actually in line with italy and  japan  the difference is in other countries  they got rich before they got old  that hasn't happened in china it's why  it's such a big headache for the chinese  government  simply hoping more people have more  babies isn't going to reverse the trend
 

